This project runs on its self-contained first-party `muse/` native Python agent runtime alongside
`companion/`, and includes, integrates with, or draws historical inspiration from the following
open-source projects:

- web/ began as the WebUI of nanobot (https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot).
  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025-present Xubin Ren and the nanobot contributors.

- Hermes Agent (https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent) powered Muse Bot v1.x and informed
  portions of the architecture and v1.x on-disk data-directory conventions (`config.yaml`,
  `memories/`, `skills/`, `cron/`, and read-only `state.db` migration compatibility; no Hermes
  source code is downloaded or bundled in v2.0+ releases).
  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research.

- Chart.js (https://www.chartjs.org), MIT License, and Leaflet (https://leafletjs.com), BSD 2-Clause
  License, bundled for interactive cards in web/public/ui-kit/vendor and
  ios/Companion/Resources/UiKit/vendor (their license files are next to them).

- Provider icons from lobe-icons (https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons), MIT License; see
  web/public/brand/provider-icons-NOTICE.txt.

- MarkdownUI (https://github.com/gonzalezreal/swift-markdown-ui), MIT License, used by the iPhone
  app as a Swift package.

- Optional local speech-to-text (muse/voice/ and companion/modules/stt_sensevoice.py) integrates with
  SenseVoice-Small (https://github.com/FunAudioLLM/SenseVoice, MIT License) and sherpa-onnx
  (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx, Apache License 2.0) when installed by the user on the
  server (neither is included in this repository or release bundles).

- The web app's npm dependencies (web/package.json) and the server's Python dependencies
  (pyproject.toml / uv.lock) are installed from their registries under their own licenses.
